{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>But as for me — Your strength</b>: Corresponding to \"his strength toward You,\" I will sing." "<b>And Your kindness</b>: Corresponding to \"O El of my kindnesses.\"" "<b>And in the morning</b>: The opposite of dogs, for by day they slumber." "<b>For You have been a refuge for me</b>: For You heard my prayer; from those who rise against me, You will shelter me."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 59, :notes {0 "Rendered hyper-literally; the Hebrew of the comment is compressed and elliptical, pairing the psalmist's 'Your strength' with the adversaries' 'his strength toward You.'", 2 "Reads כלבים ('dogs') as the enemy metaphor of the psalm; the point is that the enemies prowl at night like dogs, but the psalmist sings at morning."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:19.483858253Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}